       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum recommended metformin dose. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg PO per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n- Another dose you had in mind.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
